{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:11.991751Z","id":"cb447f5fe0799f11b5064775994815e792ac4ad4821507f0aba99a2b46404091","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: the same record as 8ff1253101ed32377473c836c3d87e9967132d3de60eef18e187c14851001dd9 (kept), re-anchored on a parallel branch.","supersedes":"69829535fefda89ac12152f1438e24e041c823c83fd04f90c8110f6a44acdbc7","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:33.800076Z","id":"b95b30060d26357905211588ddbfedffacfb7b273cd260908a114e91aa7a1d53","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs reads the alarm through GET /_worker/alarm, but every due time is a minute or more away (presence 90 s, stream grace 60 s, seat idle, grant expiry, planner refresh 1 h), so the alarm handler's sweep, grant expiry and optimize never run under test. A test route that runs the handler now, or due times shortened by test variables, would cover it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1181},"end":{"line":1199},"content_hash":"b3759215a701feeed46b3294339746437bc38573d48d3ecfc07d9aad5027b033"},"summary":"No test fires the instance's alarm: the e2e checks only when it is set","supersedes":"8ff1253101ed32377473c836c3d87e9967132d3de60eef18e187c14851001dd9","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:35:23.259667Z","id":"ea6158f906de7fc5dbbc8d30b58b7e2b3ffb0e862ebafb0159b0218ff6921e19","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:478-490 routes GET /api/events (SSE) and GET /api/toolpath/export on native targets only; the Worker's sockets (stream, live layers, room) and /mcp are served (this module's Sockets docs; routes/mod.rs wasm32 branch). daemon::reap_idle (crates/clax-server/src/daemon.rs:236) ends sessions whose local PID is gone and has no Worker counterpart, since no harness process runs beside the object. Question graces, live seats and presence across a wake are handled (this module's Alarm and 'Seats and presence across a wake' docs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"60ef33fd10c20852e2e47e1b331b875db159c339d764965c2cac79c77e62c660"},"summary":"What the daemon runs that the Worker does not: GET /api/events, GET /api/toolpath/export and the idle-session reaper","supersedes":"e2d2214a9cbb9f1423a57ac61c16e7d5eb855c6d0ac651e97246ce39023719ca","tags":["wasm","worker","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:20.453545Z","id":"b5fcac2e61b94c2b437cdd0d6b9e0cd240785e36db3deec7dc5db56f60c5c161","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:25042c18","summary":"Fixed in 25042c18: a set CLAX_TOKEN under MIN_TOKEN_CHARS (32) fails the instance's build with the reason (checked_token); the Worker's e2e and smoke scripts use longer tokens. (cd crates/clax-worker && cargo test a_set_owner_token_must_be_long_enough_to_be_unguessable): 1 passed.","supersedes":"ea1ccd0aafebd1bd1971c26c3397298cc29700e46860c38593a32f5b6789d73a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:20.479481Z","id":"2d6cf0e9e1e73c285b3dd735e8da73f4b02a2600ff0937f80d11c58bf19181e5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:608a2267","summary":"Fixed in 608a2267: ClaxDb opens its database at the first event (ClaxDb::opened); a failure answers 503 with the reason and is tried again at the next event. node crates/clax-worker/test-wasm.mjs: ok (the spike's notes, abort, fill and socket checks against the lazily opened database).","supersedes":"4c4d70000dbc6cb6c32db6ad482bb0c1dcc60aae81f1e282c73f72fc1f212753","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:02:00.420388Z","id":"2d75b2b8132ed3c94fbac22c706cb57d47f94912046f99f3482ac30f4c937b5a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ea6158f906de7fc5dbbc8d30b58b7e2b3ffb0e862ebafb0159b0218ff6921e19","summary":"Since 3fe98559 the Worker runs the session reaper from its alarm: AppState::reap_unseen ends sessions unseen for Store::REMOTE_SESSION_IDLE_SECS counted from their last request (Store::reap_sessions_from with no resume), and the alarm is set for Store::sessions_next_idle. Evidence: cargo test -p clax-core a_host_never_down_counts_remote_idle_from_the_last_request_alone passes; scripts/check-wasm.sh --manifest-path crates/clax-worker/Cargo.toml builds. No test fires the alarm (b95b3006). Still not on the Worker: GET /api/events and GET /api/toolpath/export.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.865789Z","id":"7ea92c989319c4b77e43fff1a1028788ec70fa9e6dcc0eca9b60a6f8ffd70f62","body":{"detail":"Instance::keep serializes every held seat and live presence report and writes the JSON to _clax_instance when it differs from the last write: each presence report (every tab, about every 30 s) moves a timestamp, so each costs one row write, and the row grows with the artifacts open (64 people by 16 tabs per artifact at most for presence, the seat limits for seats). Rows per artifact, or writing only seat and presence changes a viewer could see, would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":581},"end":{"line":595},"content_hash":"3490fdde295826c3fbfaf630af2fd8574f534c487f17b9628fb69bb50dbc4b23"},"summary":"The kept seats and presence are rewritten whole in the object's storage after every event that changed them, presence PUTs included","supersedes":"88fb1340c164848f494f4c3c7b60a73969a0ff7f93b0537c2c85ef20e99761e1","tags":["worker","seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
