{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:35.177500Z","id":"04dd1caa37345a5305226112e7a8e5d3c99be61bfb8059cd7ee51caa452bd057","body":{"detail":"Instance::keep serializes every held seat and live presence report and writes the JSON to _clax_instance when it differs from the last write: each presence report (every tab, about every 30 s) moves a timestamp, so each costs one row write, and the row grows with the artifacts open (64 people by 16 tabs per artifact at most for presence, the seat limits for seats). Rows per artifact, or writing only seat and presence changes a viewer could see, would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":583},"end":{"line":597},"content_hash":"3490fdde295826c3fbfaf630af2fd8574f534c487f17b9628fb69bb50dbc4b23"},"summary":"The kept seats and presence are rewritten whole in the object's storage after every event that changed them, presence PUTs included","supersedes":"7ea92c989319c4b77e43fff1a1028788ec70fa9e6dcc0eca9b60a6f8ffd70f62","tags":["worker","seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:35.239530Z","id":"b3f8aae3cd62bb0adcb7f88b3ea25e4e2ba1e067c3b276a6d7d912bdcb419146","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs reads the alarm through GET /_worker/alarm, but every due time is a minute or more away (presence 90 s, stream grace 60 s, seat idle, grant expiry, planner refresh 1 h), so the alarm handler's sweep, grant expiry and optimize never run under test. A test route that runs the handler now, or due times shortened by test variables, would cover it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1227},"end":{"line":1245},"content_hash":"b3759215a701feeed46b3294339746437bc38573d48d3ecfc07d9aad5027b033"},"summary":"No test fires the instance's alarm: the e2e checks only when it is set","supersedes":"9bd4da41d68c748101444b2706597735df1bca8786e14c67f66ba225e45f3b19","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:35.269308Z","id":"32ae62783cfd53d82c8c8b5adede71e8fffd2eb5442e6cb45c6e664780b50f42","body":{"detail":"queue plans each batch with clax_git::events::plan_batch and asks the instance to reconcile each named artifact, acking on 200 and retrying otherwise. Under wrangler dev --local the queue is simulated and receives no Artifacts event, and no test delivers a batch to it: the event body's shape (clax_git::events::event_repo) and the consumer's ack/retry are unverified. The queue clax-artifacts-events and the event subscription must be created on the account before a deploy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":207},"end":{"line":244},"content_hash":"1c08828df7803969a798a8113dc5ec971873781f1fac611c145cc908494efc6a"},"summary":"The Artifacts pushed-event queue consumer has never run against Cloudflare Queues or a real Artifacts event","supersedes":"bdac5d459d7667cbb74e7eb835ac219e79779552360b22239214ee14e880c471","tags":["revisit:a Cloudflare account with Artifacts and Queues is available","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:52:20.537078Z","id":"4a8bb2d935ba0b2a0a12a635c827c1b42ff2b83c762c04b709bce74179259b42","body":{"detail":"The Worker embeds web/dist with rust-embed for the state's web tree (the artifact page and gallery the router renders), as clax-server's own embed did before the web UI left it. clax-embedded also carries the extension, the plugin trees and the marketplaces, and its build script needs their directories; the Worker serves none of them.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":28},"content_hash":"bcdd04ddb9008ee6be7eb120f962bdbb05d3658429d4fdebff1767f26473853b"},"summary":"Link clax-embedded in the Worker instead of embedding web/dist itself","tags":["worker","layout","revisit:clax-embedded splits its web UI from the other embeds","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/diag.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:57:46.223495Z","id":"b7f82e10fc5a859ea4bace5afc75540c9d76cfdc1548ed3f4c5d871d99b9e4ee","body":{"detail":"same_secret (lines 33-40) gates the /_diag/ routes on the owner's CLAX_TOKEN (line 193). It reimplements clax_core::secret::constant_time_eq, which crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:703 and crates/clax-server/src/github.rs:95 use for the same job. base64 (lines 69-86) reimplements standard padded base64, though crates/clax-worker/Cargo.toml:28 already depends on base64 0.22. A third copy of the comparison means a fix to the shared one does not reach the diag gate.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":33},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"df5e7c87c0aa121e7170cfb1e69120a0c5bce010f6a8e51749551f9093a64f95"},"suggested_fix":"Replace same_secret with clax_core::secret::constant_time_eq(presented.as_bytes(), token.as_bytes()), and base64() with base64::engine::general_purpose::STANDARD.encode. Then drop both helpers and their tests (lines 814-825).","summary":"diag.rs hand-rolls a constant-time comparison and a base64 encoder that the workspace already provides","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/diag.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:30.507749Z","id":"16cb8463842ccc3c116d044a37928e792a4566c026f20356561f3ed179ef876e","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker/src/diag.rs:33-40 same_secret is byte-for-byte the body of crates/clax-core/src/secret.rs:74-79 constant_time_eq (pub, in pub mod secret, crates/clax-core/src/lib.rs:42); it gates /_diag/ at diag.rs:193. crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:703 and crates/clax-server/src/github.rs:95 call the shared one. diag.rs:69-86 hand-rolls padded standard base64; crates/clax-worker/Cargo.toml:28 depends on base64 0.22 and crates/clax-worker/src/repos/tokens.rs:29-30 already uses its engine. clax-core is a dependency of clax-worker (Cargo.toml:31). Minor: diag.rs holds a second copy of the comparison, not a third. Suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"b7f82e10fc5a859ea4bace5afc75540c9d76cfdc1548ed3f4c5d871d99b9e4ee","summary":"confirmed: same_secret and base64 duplicate clax_core::secret::constant_time_eq and the base64 crate the worker already depends on","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/diag.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:59:20.593487Z","id":"7e1c290791a8a8396cd1fd0e6aa79a7703d975e8e0a955d0b9d429c78ee4aa3d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:016354a7d","summary":"Fixed: diag.rs uses clax_core::secret::constant_time_eq and the base64 crate; just worker-test (fmt, tests, clippy, test-wasm.mjs) passes on main at 94ce300c6.","supersedes":"b7f82e10fc5a859ea4bace5afc75540c9d76cfdc1548ed3f4c5d871d99b9e4ee","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:15:08.354726Z","id":"c0df13be08c90f53106a24edc98dda9a2c9451e587cd5617b26663542ed2887d","body":{"detail":"erase_deleted spawns a listener on the instance's EventBus; the delete's transaction commits first (Store::delete_artifact_async), then the event is published and the erase is a subrequest to the artifact's AppDataDo. If the object is evicted in between, or the broadcast receiver lags, the store is kept. It is unreachable (MovingAppData answers NotFound for a deleted artifact before reaching the object) but holds the artifact's documents. Erasing inside the content store's delete_artifact, which the delete awaits, would close the window, at the cost of wrapping the Worker's ContentStore.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":661},"end":{"line":689},"content_hash":"1a0e0c3b9c10238bd3d651a7d8e4466f4775bbc42974ecf60e0d50a458e118ae"},"summary":"A deleted artifact's object is erased from a task listening for Event::ArtifactDeleted; an eviction between the delete and the erase, or a lagged receiver, leaves its storage","tags":["deferred-work","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T18:24:59.700514Z","id":"4f00d2f087bfd099f4f6a960f8c292eafbaff159661ba38eb65b4ef85a8ec018","body":{"detail":"websocket_message settles the object's sockets (RoomSocket::drain, then RoomCheck::stays for a Recheck) before on_text relays the message, so an Event::Access published by a request still awaiting an outbound fetch (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs delete_share awaiting git_remotes::recheck, during which the Durable Object's input gate lets the message in) closes the socket and the message is dropped. The daemon's equivalent ordering is tested (crates/clax-server/tests/api_site_access.rs stays_open after each change); the Worker's is not: InstanceDo runs only under wrangler, and crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs cannot place a message inside that await.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1367},"end":{"line":1393},"content_hash":"26470d4a1ab3207ae7992f0e91d68110275f0318dfb0be11c344aaf1933f412e"},"summary":"No test drives a Worker room socket's message arriving while a right is being lost","tags":["site-origins","tests","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:39:58.679349Z","id":"9518a7013cc4d813d1afc4173c52c3a8d89c2357a3999410056e5b2c68da655e","body":{"detail":"PUT /api/artifacts/<aid>/versions/<n>/bundle takes bodies up to clax_http::limits::BUNDLE_BODY_LIMIT (32 MiB + 64 KiB) on the daemon, and the store refuses bundles over clax_store::app_bundles::MAX_BUNDLE_BYTES (32 MiB). On the Worker, http_request refuses any body over MAX_BODY with 413 body_too_large (not bundle_too_large) before the router sees it, and BODY_BUDGET (32 MiB) caps every body held at once, so a 32 MiB bundle could never fit. GET of a bundle also reads the whole bundle into the isolate's memory (crates/clax-server/src/routes/app_bundles.rs get_bundle). Options: accept a 16 MiB cap on the Worker and say so to the app (its error is body_too_large there); raise the limit for the bundle route alone, within the isolate's 128 MB; or stream the body to R2 without buffering it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":626},"end":{"line":634},"content_hash":"93fd06e07fa9c7ae5f42dc1f336165e7c12c0e4f37cf18036065cfadb2b8f611"},"summary":"On the Worker a bundle over 16 MiB cannot be uploaded: the instance reads at most MAX_BODY (16 MiB) of any request, while the bundle cap is 32 MiB","tags":["app-push","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:26:56.718920Z","id":"f6a02713f3fe950f0eecda2fb251e87113ee34ca7ddcee572f346a2df4077551","body":{"detail":"The Worker reads them (clax_app here; crates/clax-worker/README.md lists them), but crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs passes none, so on clax.dev they must be set in wrangler.jsonc vars or with --var until a flag is added. Without APPLE_TEAM_ID and the Android pair, /.well-known/apple-app-site-association and /.well-known/assetlinks.json answer 404 and universal and app links to /a/<id>/get do not open the app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":405},"end":{"line":425},"content_hash":"b382b7207445353e62c6f3b2e32f68f802c9f8d84126546ccd4f4c3231fc7093"},"summary":"deploy.mjs has no flags for APPLE_TEAM_ID, ANDROID_PACKAGE, ANDROID_SHA256, IOS_STORE_URL and ANDROID_STORE_URL","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.101632Z","id":"3a794794bc54c0cfcd0ee061b685a888f32597db9aa33013aaa1738f30d641c2","body":{"detail":"clax_app(env) runs while the instance's object is built (line 482, `?`), so a typo in APPLE_TEAM_ID, ANDROID_SHA256 (e.g. a fingerprint pasted without colons) or a store URL fails every request to the hosted instance after a deploy, and crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs checks none of these values before deploying (it passes none of them). The daemon refuses the same config at start-up, where the operator sees it at once.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":411},"end":{"line":425},"content_hash":"1ab79276a7f3d8689f0e5aead746b0bdaa0c1b44cd758e068a703a8b53451f3b"},"suggested_fix":"Validate the five vars in deploy.mjs (or a pre-deploy wrangler dry run that builds ClaxApp::from_settings), or log the error and serve with ClaxApp::default() on the Worker.","summary":"A malformed app-link var stops the whole instance, not just its well-known files","tags":["worker","deploy","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/bot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:17:22.420819Z","id":"8225061118ab5bca6255ba4ba3777e49b1edee00503fc4aa97618a829026006f","body":{"detail":"alarm_budget gives run_until_idle ALARM_WALL_LIMIT less ALARM_MARGIN. The object's own CPU in that time (SQLite commits through the VFS, SSE parsing of the model's stream, step payloads) is believed to stay well under Cloudflare's default 30 s per invocation, since the ticks mostly wait on the network and scripts run in their own isolates, but no run on a deployed Worker has measured it; wrangler dev --local enforces no CPU limit. Past it the invocation ends, the run resumes from its uncommitted step at the next alarm (RESUME_AFTER), and the cut model call is billed once, so the cost is a retry, not a lost run.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":84},"end":{"line":88},"content_hash":"b51e5b9a7d6cfc59c914d4d822bc4ff3a895a44a2bd29385bdcf6d3f7afe1103"},"suggested_fix":"Measure CPU per alarm on a deployment (Workers Logs' cpuTime for alarm invocations) with a long run; if it nears 30 s, set limits.cpu_ms in wrangler.jsonc or shorten the budget.","summary":"The alarm budget (10 min of wall time) is sized by the alarm's 15-minute wall limit alone; the 30 s of CPU an invocation has by default is assumed, never measured","tags":["hosted","unverified-on-cloudflare","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:17:22.420908Z","id":"de67a50b0618528caeaf5047c6f716d5ecda15598a2a598727429bd1f67d29bb","body":{"detail":"While it drives, the alarm keeps the object's alarm about a minute ahead (WorkerBot::due, renewed by the timed loop every RESUME_AFTER/2). test-bot.mjs kills wrangler mid-turn and restarts it, but there a request resumes the run (it GETs the run first). Not observed on Cloudflare: that an alarm set from inside a running alarm() survives an eviction or a CPU-limit kill and fires, and how it interacts with the platform's own retry of a failed alarm invocation.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1346},"end":{"line":1371},"content_hash":"9fda16a11fb191de9f351ef5c2691d41ce7a78c67231e4ea026eb38b595d2ca8"},"summary":"Resuming after an alarm invocation the platform ends relies on the alarm set during it (RESUME_AFTER ahead) firing in the next incarnation; only a killed wrangler dev has shown a resume, and there a request resumed it","tags":["hosted","unverified-on-cloudflare","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:17:22.420966Z","id":"e00f242417567f11528f2a609cc961dd994982afcddb52c833b1a13e92fdc4fe","body":{"detail":"GET /api/bot/runs/<id>/events is the router's streaming SSE body (clax_server::routes::bot::events), served from the Durable Object as a ReadableStream. An open stream keeps the object awake (billed duration) for the run's life, its waits included (a model retry waits 30 s, a stalled sandbox up to 60 s), where a hibernatable socket would let it sleep between steps. Kept because the web UI reads the stream with fetch and Last-Event-ID (web/shell/src/bot/api.ts), the stream ends with its run (bounded by max_run_minutes), and the object is awake for the alarm while the run ticks anyway.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":98},"end":{"line":111},"content_hash":"37a046781b0bbfee762d21d0b837b53877439bc5a1b493eaa869238a9172957e"},"summary":"Serve a run's events over a hibernatable WebSocket, as the Worker serves /api/stream, instead of the router's SSE response from the object","tags":["hosted","revisit:runs commonly wait minutes between steps, or DO duration billing shows open run streams","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:17:22.421048Z","id":"e71e43def3e73c23b4aab6d69166697a3cea52847d118fd7ae2e2a4e6a5e972a","body":{"detail":"The Worker reads no config.toml, and the instance settings in the database have no enabled switch; turning ClaxBot off for everyone on a deployment means turning each person's claxbot flag off, or leaving the instance key unset. Should a var (CLAX_BOT=0) or a stored setting turn it off?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":442},"end":{"line":450},"content_hash":"b4f525ec46bd9c2960248cb6d9403c0dd5169a62d320460e5f941f031693c4a9"},"summary":"A hosted Worker always runs ClaxBot (Bot::enabled is true): there is no var to turn it off, where the daemon has [bot] enabled","tags":["hosted","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:17:22.421477Z","id":"6405197a2bd17fc36551e97ee1283d11baace3810ca4f63ff5c4f9d57c33cffa","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"b3f8aae3cd62bb0adcb7f88b3ea25e4e2ba1e067c3b276a6d7d912bdcb419146","summary":"crates/clax-worker/test-bot.mjs now fires the alarm: every ClaxBot step there runs from alarm() (a send sets it for now, InstanceDo::schedule), and the run finishes, resumes after a restart and is cancelled through it. The instance's own timed work in alarm() (sweep, grants, reaper, planner) still has no check of its effect; a close is the owner's once one does.","tags":["evidence","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:18:19.674854Z","id":"143bd80b91b5659523de40238c63fe88cbe09520ba21eb6c0023f5c796d6e16d","body":{"detail":"last_optimize starts at construction and wrote at false, so each eviction restarts the hour and forgets the write. Keeping the time of the last refresh in the _clax_instance table would fix it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":255},"end":{"line":259},"content_hash":"600dd0ea2618052984d2503af9cce895580a8e46338c01b2c421c8e4645d0d1b"},"summary":"The planner refresh's clock and the 'a request wrote' flag live in memory: an object evicted within the hour after each write never refreshes the planner","supersedes":"b8051be3ac52f8c155135493995c83f312f1c7ca5582a5f1634291573a831e1e","tags":["review","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:18:19.694912Z","id":"b02ae950c5bc8e76e712b9076a32ef75dddb65657faf8153b762ef39d59819c2","body":{"detail":"Instance::keep serializes every held seat and live presence report and writes the JSON to _clax_instance when it differs from the last write: each presence report (every tab, about every 30 s) moves a timestamp, so each costs one row write, and the row grows with the artifacts open (64 people by 16 tabs per artifact at most for presence, the seat limits for seats). Rows per artifact, or writing only seat and presence changes a viewer could see, would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":654},"end":{"line":668},"content_hash":"ed3dec1014cfe30f372f43d143aab32f821dab4ccf7f196f568ad19f8115956f"},"summary":"The kept seats and presence are rewritten whole in the object's storage after every event that changed them, presence PUTs included","supersedes":"04dd1caa37345a5305226112e7a8e5d3c99be61bfb8059cd7ee51caa452bd057","tags":["worker","seats","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:18:19.714223Z","id":"e732281018afada54fa8a0cd8fa90b39ba9afb2bd8c12a534f15aff5d286754e","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs reads the alarm through GET /_worker/alarm, but every due time is a minute or more away (presence 90 s, stream grace 60 s, seat idle, grant expiry, planner refresh 1 h), so the alarm handler's sweep, grant expiry and optimize never run under test. A test route that runs the handler now, or due times shortened by test variables, would cover it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1338},"end":{"line":1376},"content_hash":"70637541b423a26a48955aa04758ba85fade7b03fc867b915a346e9ce46f5b84"},"summary":"No test fires the instance's alarm: the e2e checks only when it is set","supersedes":"b3f8aae3cd62bb0adcb7f88b3ea25e4e2ba1e067c3b276a6d7d912bdcb419146","tags":["review","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:20:33.017304Z","id":"91718b49405f94b079a9a0babcf65de369a7c8ee0f0e4b2d25c26c46a3b30986","body":{"detail":"Instance::keep serializes every held seat and live presence report and writes the JSON to _clax_instance when it differs from the last write: each presence report (every tab, about every 30 s) moves a timestamp, so each costs one row write, and the row grows with the artifacts open (64 people by 16 tabs per artifact at most for presence, the seat limits for seats). Rows per artifact, or writing only seat and presence changes a viewer could see, would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":653},"end":{"line":667},"content_hash":"ed3dec1014cfe30f372f43d143aab32f821dab4ccf7f196f568ad19f8115956f"},"summary":"The kept seats and presence are rewritten whole in the object's storage after every event that changed them, presence PUTs included","supersedes":"b02ae950c5bc8e76e712b9076a32ef75dddb65657faf8153b762ef39d59819c2","tags":["worker","seats","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:20:33.037987Z","id":"b13a6e96c2173beb23701b0eb9d30ca9cd542ac1b317e7b97e25183a91a14f1b","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs reads the alarm through GET /_worker/alarm, but every due time is a minute or more away (presence 90 s, stream grace 60 s, seat idle, grant expiry, planner refresh 1 h), so the alarm handler's sweep, grant expiry and optimize never run under test. A test route that runs the handler now, or due times shortened by test variables, would cover it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1341},"end":{"line":1382},"content_hash":"abf2c073518908e09f3ed4f631e8af244b11c9072cbac9d445508605fd3efa53"},"summary":"No test fires the instance's alarm: the e2e checks only when it is set","supersedes":"e732281018afada54fa8a0cd8fa90b39ba9afb2bd8c12a534f15aff5d286754e","tags":["review","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:20:33.059407Z","id":"ff81a699e5f1adf93b9c3c03b7081390750527aecbd7f32004c672ae172b9a3f","body":{"detail":"While it drives, the alarm keeps the object's alarm about a minute ahead (WorkerBot::due, renewed by the timed loop every RESUME_AFTER/2). test-bot.mjs kills wrangler mid-turn and restarts it, but there a request resumes the run (it GETs the run first). Not observed on Cloudflare: that an alarm set from inside a running alarm() survives an eviction or a CPU-limit kill and fires, and how it interacts with the platform's own retry of a failed alarm invocation.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1349},"end":{"line":1378},"content_hash":"6fe3af240936dfc6a5301a5c8a231aab51d47104a69316fdd537c7fccd11fbaf"},"summary":"Resuming after an alarm invocation the platform ends relies on the alarm set during it (RESUME_AFTER ahead) firing in the next incarnation; only a killed wrangler dev has shown a resume, and there a request resumed it","supersedes":"de67a50b0618528caeaf5047c6f716d5ecda15598a2a598727429bd1f67d29bb","tags":["hosted","unverified-on-cloudflare","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/bot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:15:16.346493Z","id":"961e2174bdfa061aded2856c36f6c09fc3a90abd3ded7690c646e561f34ffbe5","body":{"detail":"alarm_budget gives run_until_idle ALARM_WALL_LIMIT less ALARM_MARGIN. The object's own CPU in that time (SQLite commits through the VFS, SSE parsing of the model's stream, step payloads) is believed to stay well under Cloudflare's default 30 s per invocation, since the ticks mostly wait on the network and scripts run in their own isolates, but no run on a deployed Worker has measured it; wrangler dev --local enforces no CPU limit. Past it the invocation ends, the run resumes from its uncommitted step at the next alarm (RESUME_AFTER), and the cut model call is billed once, so the cost is a retry, not a lost run.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":91},"end":{"line":95},"content_hash":"b51e5b9a7d6cfc59c914d4d822bc4ff3a895a44a2bd29385bdcf6d3f7afe1103"},"suggested_fix":"Measure CPU per alarm on a deployment (Workers Logs' cpuTime for alarm invocations) with a long run; if it nears 30 s, set limits.cpu_ms in wrangler.jsonc or shorten the budget.","summary":"The alarm budget (10 min of wall time) is sized by the alarm's 15-minute wall limit alone; the 30 s of CPU an invocation has by default is assumed, never measured","supersedes":"8225061118ab5bca6255ba4ba3777e49b1edee00503fc4aa97618a829026006f","tags":["hosted","unverified-on-cloudflare","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:15:16.368932Z","id":"1e8c25366bd203b4463d56e7bc8cbae4c16d142a60ee24a8c742ba8a2a6cc4fa","body":{"detail":"Instance::keep serializes every held seat and live presence report and writes the JSON to _clax_instance when it differs from the last write: each presence report (every tab, about every 30 s) moves a timestamp, so each costs one row write, and the row grows with the artifacts open (64 people by 16 tabs per artifact at most for presence, the seat limits for seats). Rows per artifact, or writing only seat and presence changes a viewer could see, would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":678},"end":{"line":692},"content_hash":"ed3dec1014cfe30f372f43d143aab32f821dab4ccf7f196f568ad19f8115956f"},"summary":"The kept seats and presence are rewritten whole in the object's storage after every event that changed them, presence PUTs included","supersedes":"91718b49405f94b079a9a0babcf65de369a7c8ee0f0e4b2d25c26c46a3b30986","tags":["worker","seats","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:15:16.390038Z","id":"dd5911c49a3373cf2dfbc720fbeb0c2e5006c897f97e9d01e6b3e90f198819be","body":{"detail":"worker_bot sets enabled from whether crate::bot::sandbox could be made. The daemon has [bot] enabled; the Worker reads no config.toml and the stored instance settings have no switch, so turning ClaxBot off for everyone means turning each person's claxbot flag off or leaving the instance key unset. Should a var (CLAX_BOT=0) or a stored setting turn it off?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":432},"end":{"line":477},"content_hash":"69ff8c3cdbf0b9c0478de8075c7fba554b79900435ab9277f8c9f0bfe2195a91"},"summary":"No setting turns ClaxBot off on a hosted Worker: only a sandbox that cannot be made does (Bot::enabled false, sends refused not_configured)","supersedes":"e71e43def3e73c23b4aab6d69166697a3cea52847d118fd7ae2e2a4e6a5e972a","tags":["hosted","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:15:16.411779Z","id":"959373a163528fcb396ab1c9e391344146e5a9bb0a959053b66e8fa745fa3b2e","body":{"kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1367},"end":{"line":1409},"content_hash":"b9cc80259e2ad339f471213a9935fae8f9781b9232374cf6ec8dca34bfe0ef42"},"summary":"No test fires the instance's alarm: the e2e checks only when it is set","supersedes":"b13a6e96c2173beb23701b0eb9d30ca9cd542ac1b317e7b97e25183a91a14f1b","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:15:16.434252Z","id":"b2107409c941e699f75dab75c8ab35c38aa745a1cc646b2688bbf5c4d76c9731","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker/test-bot.mjs kills wrangler while a turn streams and restarts it with no request to the instance: the alarm, kept CLAX_TEST_RESUME_AFTER_MS (3 s) ahead, fires in the new incarnation and resumes the run. Not observed on Cloudflare: that an alarm set from inside a running alarm() survives an eviction or a CPU-limit kill and fires, and how it interacts with the platform's own retry of a failed alarm invocation.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1375},"end":{"line":1405},"content_hash":"766cf220a681f32e8f1df01268223fa7723e8e067fa6d35fcc16607145e524d8"},"summary":"Resuming after an alarm invocation the platform ends relies on the alarm set during it (kept RESUME_AFTER ahead) firing in the next incarnation; shown only under wrangler dev --local","supersedes":"ff81a699e5f1adf93b9c3c03b7081390750527aecbd7f32004c672ae172b9a3f","tags":["hosted","unverified-on-cloudflare","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/bot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:15:16.476334Z","id":"acfcc20a0e2db4261a4c60dd597f237bc91c21849fc5be69cd707d5774148b38","body":{"detail":"start(true) takes each live run's claim back at once. It is safe on the Worker: the runs are in the object's own storage, which one incarnation writes at a time, and an old incarnation still finishing a step finds its claim gone at its next renewal or write (Wait::NotOurs) and commits nothing. With start(false) a run cut by an eviction waits out the dead driver's lease (lease_secs, 60 s) and the 30 s NOT_OURS_WAIT before it resumes.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":369},"end":{"line":381},"content_hash":"d0b650aef0db575ad4b08cd69214e00f07d9ae0aaba63702d603d8097c0ac6d1"},"summary":"Start the Worker's driver with Driver::start(false), leaving earlier incarnations' claims to lapse, instead of start(true)","tags":["hosted","revisit:Cloudflare runs two live incarnations of one object at once","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:57:56.645341Z","id":"5bd9efcd3845ca90a0e5b057ae63775508dfc9258bf8770982ba2124d54e7771","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"959373a163528fcb396ab1c9e391344146e5a9bb0a959053b66e8fa745fa3b2e","summary":"Evidence for a close: crates/clax-worker/test-bot.mjs (since 88645653) fires the alarm with no request at all: wrangler is killed mid-turn and restarted, and only the instance's alarm (kept CLAX_TEST_RESUME_AFTER_MS ahead) resumes the run, which finishes; it also checks the alarm kept ahead and renewed while it drives, and through /_worker/alarm's bot field that none is held once every run ended (node test-bot.mjs --no-build: all checks ok, three runs). The instance's own timed work run from alarm() (sweep, grants, reaper, planner) is exercised in those alarms but its effect is not asserted. Proposing the owner close this.","tags":["evidence","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
