{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:43:26.365256Z","id":"9e440a4b05ae483ab369264381286652bbf2f479cfc15b7c3781edc237fc4ad3","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker/test-bot.mjs kills wrangler while a turn streams and restarts it with no request to the instance: the alarm, kept CLAX_TEST_RESUME_AFTER_MS (3 s) ahead, fires in the new incarnation and resumes the run. Not observed on Cloudflare: that an alarm set from inside a running alarm() survives an eviction or a CPU-limit kill and fires, and how it interacts with the platform's own retry of a failed alarm invocation.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1378},"end":{"line":1408},"content_hash":"766cf220a681f32e8f1df01268223fa7723e8e067fa6d35fcc16607145e524d8"},"summary":"Resuming after an alarm invocation the platform ends relies on the alarm set during it (kept RESUME_AFTER ahead) firing in the next incarnation; shown only under wrangler dev --local","supersedes":"b2107409c941e699f75dab75c8ab35c38aa745a1cc646b2688bbf5c4d76c9731","tags":["hosted","unverified-on-cloudflare","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:43:26.385759Z","id":"21f90c9286a71fad337f16050bc01368ef5ed3e2edae364fabd7c7dd9c4c3229","body":{"detail":"worker_bot sets enabled from whether crate::bot::sandbox could be made. The daemon has [bot] enabled; the Worker reads no config.toml and the stored instance settings have no switch, so turning ClaxBot off for everyone means turning each person's claxbot flag off or leaving the instance key unset. Should a var (CLAX_BOT=0) or a stored setting turn it off?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":432},"end":{"line":480},"content_hash":"7d7a9779bbf6ed08d0d56ea52f9e9af03e67bcce5b3c08590b21128b7091416a"},"summary":"No setting turns ClaxBot off on a hosted Worker: only a sandbox that cannot be made does (Bot::enabled false, sends refused not_configured)","supersedes":"dd5911c49a3373cf2dfbc720fbeb0c2e5006c897f97e9d01e6b3e90f198819be","tags":["hosted","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.296750Z","id":"2d5ddc9a9d8387e9852652131f37e4b5980fe9ec4c981415cb42dc26e31f8d02","body":{"detail":"queue plans each batch with clax_git::events::plan_batch and asks the instance to reconcile each named artifact, acking on 200 and retrying otherwise. Under wrangler dev --local the queue is simulated and receives no Artifacts event, and no test delivers a batch to it: the event body's shape (clax_git::events::event_repo) and the consumer's ack/retry are unverified. The queue clax-artifacts-events and the event subscription must be created on the account before a deploy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":210},"end":{"line":247},"content_hash":"1c08828df7803969a798a8113dc5ec971873781f1fac611c145cc908494efc6a"},"summary":"The Artifacts pushed-event queue consumer has never run against Cloudflare Queues or a real Artifacts event","supersedes":"32ae62783cfd53d82c8c8b5adede71e8fffd2eb5442e6cb45c6e664780b50f42","tags":["revisit:a Cloudflare account with Artifacts and Queues is available","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
