{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:09.567657Z","id":"384184b72952d22ddf71d3ff165e322d63cdd264e4564628af6aabb03a9a077c","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker/test-bot.mjs kills wrangler while a turn streams and restarts it with no request to the instance: the alarm, kept CLAX_TEST_RESUME_AFTER_MS (3 s) ahead, fires in the new incarnation and resumes the run. Not observed on Cloudflare: that an alarm set from inside a running alarm() survives an eviction or a CPU-limit kill and fires, and how it interacts with the platform's own retry of a failed alarm invocation.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1380},"end":{"line":1410},"content_hash":"766cf220a681f32e8f1df01268223fa7723e8e067fa6d35fcc16607145e524d8"},"summary":"Resuming after an alarm invocation the platform ends relies on the alarm set during it (kept RESUME_AFTER ahead) firing in the next incarnation; shown only under wrangler dev --local","supersedes":"9e440a4b05ae483ab369264381286652bbf2f479cfc15b7c3781edc237fc4ad3","tags":["hosted","unverified-on-cloudflare","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:09.622706Z","id":"f2ace00be4bceb1f8d882d33d3dd7b45813bbfc5f2d670e1a6cbad5b7871a61a","body":{"detail":"Instance::keep serializes every held seat and live presence report and writes the JSON to _clax_instance when it differs from the last write: each presence report (every tab, about every 30 s) moves a timestamp, so each costs one row write, and the row grows with the artifacts open (64 people by 16 tabs per artifact at most for presence, the seat limits for seats). Rows per artifact, or writing only seat and presence changes a viewer could see, would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":683},"end":{"line":697},"content_hash":"ed3dec1014cfe30f372f43d143aab32f821dab4ccf7f196f568ad19f8115956f"},"summary":"The kept seats and presence are rewritten whole in the object's storage after every event that changed them, presence PUTs included","supersedes":"05f6e9e7cb18f440f753cede8884e87853261af3730e94867bbb518479e6c38d","tags":["worker","seats","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:14.031649Z","id":"74d9f2a3552904aa22c5a4a9c48aaceb1e81bfa80ce89e15986ea22676d3769c","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:478-490 routes GET /api/events (SSE) and GET /api/toolpath/export on native targets only; the Worker's sockets (stream, live layers, room) and /mcp are served (this module's Sockets docs; routes/mod.rs wasm32 branch). daemon::reap_idle (crates/clax-server/src/daemon.rs:236) ends sessions whose local PID is gone and has no Worker counterpart, since no harness process runs beside the object. Question graces, live seats and presence across a wake are handled (this module's Alarm and 'Seats and presence across a wake' docs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"0fad33a774314e7385217af99e1cad28f44bec964c62de5e0d6ce57337354227"},"summary":"What the daemon runs that the Worker does not: GET /api/events, GET /api/toolpath/export and the idle-session reaper","supersedes":"ea6158f906de7fc5dbbc8d30b58b7e2b3ffb0e862ebafb0159b0218ff6921e19","tags":["wasm","worker","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:14.980848Z","id":"0a0c1a6abe1df34fd8a23eb8d155c74a28d3a1f112d44e8e460ff686a57fe027","body":{"detail":"websocket_message settles the object's sockets (RoomSocket::drain, then RoomCheck::stays for a Recheck) before on_text relays the message, so an Event::Access published by a request still awaiting an outbound fetch (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs delete_share awaiting git_remotes::recheck, during which the Durable Object's input gate lets the message in) closes the socket and the message is dropped. The daemon's equivalent ordering is tested (crates/clax-server/tests/api_site_access.rs stays_open after each change); the Worker's is not: InstanceDo runs only under wrangler, and crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs cannot place a message inside that await.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1517},"end":{"line":1543},"content_hash":"26470d4a1ab3207ae7992f0e91d68110275f0318dfb0be11c344aaf1933f412e"},"summary":"No test drives a Worker room socket's message arriving while a right is being lost","supersedes":"4f00d2f087bfd099f4f6a960f8c292eafbaff159661ba38eb65b4ef85a8ec018","tags":["site-origins","tests","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:16.295107Z","id":"37389f7d197c0d59526e02a84bbbcb20a24fb0d5565d45e71ee37f5a233f8814","body":{"detail":"GET /api/bot/runs/<id>/events is the router's streaming SSE body (clax_server::routes::bot::events), served from the Durable Object as a ReadableStream. An open stream keeps the object awake (billed duration) for the run's life, its waits included (a model retry waits 30 s, a stalled sandbox up to 60 s), where a hibernatable socket would let it sleep between steps. Kept because the web UI reads the stream with fetch and Last-Event-ID (web/shell/src/bot/api.ts), the stream ends with its run (bounded by max_run_minutes), and the object is awake for the alarm while the run ticks anyway.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":98},"end":{"line":111},"content_hash":"28745a215b805b6db2d66d11b7d02e3da170be3450534382395b04f40008e404"},"summary":"Serve a run's events over a hibernatable WebSocket, as the Worker serves /api/stream, instead of the router's SSE response from the object","supersedes":"e00f242417567f11528f2a609cc961dd994982afcddb52c833b1a13e92fdc4fe","tags":["hosted","revisit:runs commonly wait minutes between steps, or DO duration billing shows open run streams","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:17.359960Z","id":"efa180be2ddeb525984ce22305f228719c6f894864e990c78f25262eb0e7596b","body":{"detail":"last_optimize starts at construction and wrote at false, so each eviction restarts the hour and forgets the write. Keeping the time of the last refresh in the _clax_instance table would fix it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":272},"end":{"line":276},"content_hash":"4acc92ea01287018bd29ad7eaa113c22c875790c12ba377f7c8dce2f271624b1"},"summary":"The planner refresh's clock and the 'a request wrote' flag live in memory: an object evicted within the hour after each write never refreshes the planner","supersedes":"143bd80b91b5659523de40238c63fe88cbe09520ba21eb6c0023f5c796d6e16d","tags":["review","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:17.858869Z","id":"8b54910c414c8306162844a08e7fdb89055139ac0f28ee0db5fe00d7523f488f","body":{"detail":"queue plans each batch with clax_git::events::plan_batch and asks the instance to reconcile each named artifact, acking on 200 and retrying otherwise. Under wrangler dev --local the queue is simulated and receives no Artifacts event, and no test delivers a batch to it: the event body's shape (clax_git::events::event_repo) and the consumer's ack/retry are unverified. The queue clax-artifacts-events and the event subscription must be created on the account before a deploy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":223},"end":{"line":260},"content_hash":"3da7572e987ad0cc995dacb30a98311c2e99249e569dfeefda7048ee69087f9f"},"summary":"The Artifacts pushed-event queue consumer has never run against Cloudflare Queues or a real Artifacts event","supersedes":"2d5ddc9a9d8387e9852652131f37e4b5980fe9ec4c981415cb42dc26e31f8d02","tags":["revisit:a Cloudflare account with Artifacts and Queues is available","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T00:31:21.317269Z","id":"ad2563df516b127fe027b253441fbf63d7df27f66b833fd74d98dd936f44db00","body":{"detail":"on_text returns RoomSocket::renewal's RoomCheck and the caller renews it (instance.rs:1539), mirroring the daemon's renewal tested in crates/clax-server/tests/api_site_access.rs:1686-1706. Neither the Worker's unit tests nor crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs advance time past SITE_SESSION_RENEW_SECS (crates/clax-store/src/site_sessions.rs:33) with an active socket, so a hosted session can expire under a socket in use without any check failing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1676},"end":{"line":1722},"content_hash":"c353f16f9d2143c228b7e3f01f409dbf3901ada4dfc2c7091e08c5fafcd75301"},"summary":"No test exercises the Worker's site session renewal on room socket activity","tags":["test-coverage","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/diag.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:37:55.676627Z","id":"67a110bdb961fdd2610526a4ff317ced0fd3bb13ddd1ea012a127189fd7a97fb","body":{"detail":"The diagnostics run only in a deployed Worker with CLAX_DIAG_ROUTES=1 (crates/clax-worker/smoke-remote.mjs), so the owner_reaches check before reconcile_pushes (as on repos/token and artifacts/tree) is covered by the wasm build (just worker-test: clippy and test-wasm.mjs) and not by a request. A test would call it with CLAX_TOKEN for an artifact a person made and expect 404 and no recorded push.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":240},"end":{"line":256},"content_hash":"55cfd260d1dc710d052a986cbaea60e245837ef9b324631568c052392c154a02"},"summary":"No automated test covers POST /_diag/reconcile?artifact= answering 404 for an artifact out of the owner's reach","tags":["hosted","test-gap","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:45:52.649821Z","id":"0a403dd526ec373e351d15faa71cbcb13c5ffeda37f2ba50cedf93a8842e4720","body":{"kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":207},"end":{"line":244},"content_hash":"04c5c3f15a245248dba8f96d9db280ce65a902db1feab6c22e5be075fbd7e2a7"},"summary":"x","tags":["session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
