{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:45.722098Z","id":"0c6266f196233745756665df0aaffe6581ab5c2b700d7a727445180e013e6622","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs reads the alarm through GET /_worker/alarm, but every due time is a minute or more away (presence 90 s, stream grace 60 s, seat idle, grant expiry, planner refresh 1 h), so the alarm handler's sweep, grant expiry and optimize never run under test. A test route that runs the handler now, or due times shortened by test variables, would cover it.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs:1227:1245 to crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs:1252:1270: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1252},"end":{"line":1270},"content_hash":"b3759215a701feeed46b3294339746437bc38573d48d3ecfc07d9aad5027b033"},"summary":"No test fires the instance's alarm: the e2e checks only when it is set","supersedes":"b3f8aae3cd62bb0adcb7f88b3ea25e4e2ba1e067c3b276a6d7d912bdcb419146","tags":["review","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
