{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:08.605745Z","id":"fffcc35e070e334b3f4e25e6c73393668343ae65d2b29c47f593e6af5f567015","body":{"detail":"Instance::keep serializes every held seat and live presence report and writes the JSON to _clax_instance when it differs from the last write: each presence report (every tab, about every 30 s) moves a timestamp, so each costs one row write, and the row grows with the artifacts open (64 people by 16 tabs per artifact at most for presence, the seat limits for seats). Rows per artifact, or writing only seat and presence changes a viewer could see, would bound it.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs:583:597 to crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs:601:615: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":730},"end":{"line":744},"content_hash":"3490fdde295826c3fbfaf630af2fd8574f534c487f17b9628fb69bb50dbc4b23"},"summary":"The kept seats and presence are rewritten whole in the object's storage after every event that changed them, presence PUTs included","supersedes":"9d56f360789be2cbf75fc7a371573364e320e87509eca7aceb3024af1615e098","tags":["worker","seats","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:08.675081Z","id":"47483335bbc864c36b40a1fc48a929ddbe69e2d08632a88f70b4dad960573544","body":{"detail":"queue plans each batch with clax_git::events::plan_batch and asks the instance to reconcile each named artifact, acking on 200 and retrying otherwise. Under wrangler dev --local the queue is simulated and receives no Artifacts event, and no test delivers a batch to it: the event body's shape (clax_git::events::event_repo) and the consumer's ack/retry are unverified. The queue clax-artifacts-events and the event subscription must be created on the account before a deploy.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs:207:244 to crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs:228:265: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":231},"end":{"line":268},"content_hash":"1c08828df7803969a798a8113dc5ec971873781f1fac611c145cc908494efc6a"},"summary":"The Artifacts pushed-event queue consumer has never run against Cloudflare Queues or a real Artifacts event","supersedes":"8cad76fbdc9de53fb1e480b72205898fcbd12b292e623fd0c982df2b2073aa56","tags":["revisit:a Cloudflare account with Artifacts and Queues is available","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:09.214448Z","id":"1dd61f69ae810d8c6b229c01654f38f6932431043b9b1f0610773a4bfbeb7e00","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"A placeholder concern with the summary \"x\" and no detail, recorded by this session by mistake; it names no finding.","supersedes":"0a403dd526ec373e351d15faa71cbcb13c5ffeda37f2ba50cedf93a8842e4720","tags":["reason:invalid","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T14:57:10.418225Z","id":"2d28b38dc1aa908467d89839ef1c021dc377d1bb6bae08c0eed54ab32b74411e","body":{"detail":"GET /api/bot/runs/<id>/events is the router's streaming SSE body (clax_server::routes::bot::events), served from the Durable Object as a ReadableStream. An open stream keeps the object awake (billed duration) for the run's life, its waits included (a model retry waits 30 s, a stalled sandbox up to 60 s), where a hibernatable socket would let it sleep between steps. Kept because the web UI reads the stream with fetch and Last-Event-ID (web/shell/src/bot/api.ts), the stream ends with its run (bounded by max_run_minutes), and the object is awake for the alarm while the run ticks anyway.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":103},"end":{"line":116},"content_hash":"28745a215b805b6db2d66d11b7d02e3da170be3450534382395b04f40008e404"},"summary":"Serve a run's events over a hibernatable WebSocket, as the Worker serves /api/stream, instead of the router's SSE response from the object","supersedes":"37389f7d197c0d59526e02a84bbbcb20a24fb0d5565d45e71ee37f5a233f8814","tags":["hosted","revisit:runs commonly wait minutes between steps, or DO duration billing shows open run streams","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T14:57:10.493108Z","id":"17ac9696af7ecb81e7d877cc092cba2a8f228f3d66c2829d3b45f2633a483bee","body":{"detail":"last_optimize starts at construction and wrote at false, so each eviction restarts the hour and forgets the write. Keeping the time of the last refresh in the _clax_instance table would fix it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":277},"end":{"line":281},"content_hash":"4acc92ea01287018bd29ad7eaa113c22c875790c12ba377f7c8dce2f271624b1"},"summary":"The planner refresh's clock and the 'a request wrote' flag live in memory: an object evicted within the hour after each write never refreshes the planner","supersedes":"efa180be2ddeb525984ce22305f228719c6f894864e990c78f25262eb0e7596b","tags":["review","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
