{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:01:33.059141Z","id":"359b42de6b3fd1bed62060c60fb403208fc657e63f06f568cc467b2ab634f471","body":{"detail":"forward_undeclared and Relay (52c9c3efd) fix the 500 that `node scripts/e2e-hosted.mjs` gave for \"a chunked body past 96 MiB is refused 413\" (3/30 and 5/15 repeats before, with workerd's \"Can't read from request stream after response has been sent\"; 30/30 answered 413 after, and the whole hosted e2e passed, 94 ok). That run is workerd under wrangler dev; the production runtime's handling of a cancelled request stream behind a relayed body has not been exercised. Relay also copies each chunk into a new Uint8Array (worker::ByteStream yields Vec<u8>), one extra copy per chunk of an upload of no declared length.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":242},"end":{"line":286},"content_hash":"80f9a0d791abf2a9646bbfb13b466c3f3f8c5aead5db458cd71646dba5508c10"},"summary":"The relay of a body with no declared length is proven under wrangler dev only, not on Cloudflare, and copies every chunk once","tags":["risk","revisit:after-first-hosted-deploy","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T02:27:30.517094Z","id":"504538bb873ec206cc5a334e2f28fa13af94ae8a9b52d046e033086175e18df1","body":{"detail":"instance.rs:660 builds app.quickstart from the web build on every Worker (no setting turns it off). crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs and the other Worker e2e scripts were not run with seeding on; one that counts a new person's artifacts or lists their gallery would see one more (the pinned Clax Quickstart). wasm32 check of clax-server and clax-store passes (just check-wasm -p clax-server, -p clax-store).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":658},"end":{"line":660},"content_hash":"5ff5998a056a2b39f9d37ea22e0bf5868793af5365dde828ceb109d4d12b32cb"},"summary":"The Worker always seeds the quickstart, with no switch, and its e2e scripts were not run with seeding on","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:10.126643Z","id":"0a2ec7f3927feb29c64d8638c5a55a612adc5205be9001a5cbd6b1fdac4ca87a","body":{"detail":"instance.rs:660 builds app.quickstart from the web build on every Worker (no setting turns it off). crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs and the other Worker e2e scripts were not run with seeding on; one that counts a new person's artifacts or lists their gallery would see one more (the pinned Clax Quickstart). wasm32 check of clax-server and clax-store passes (just check-wasm -p clax-server, -p clax-store).\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from the record 504538bb (mailto:alex@kesling.co, session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7) onto the lines it concerns, which moved when crates/clax-worker joined the root workspace and Bazel's build.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":671},"end":{"line":673},"content_hash":"5ff5998a056a2b39f9d37ea22e0bf5868793af5365dde828ceb109d4d12b32cb"},"summary":"The Worker always seeds the quickstart, with no switch, and its e2e scripts were not run with seeding on","supersedes":"504538bb873ec206cc5a334e2f28fa13af94ae8a9b52d046e033086175e18df1","tags":["review","session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:10.240275Z","id":"f87fc62745f4c4c35a3b93ac4ac7c88842d151b9e10ea92e0cd78655789efbf6","body":{"detail":"The Worker embeds web/dist with rust-embed for the state's web tree (the artifact page and gallery the router renders), as clax-server's own embed did before the web UI left it. clax-embedded also carries the extension, the plugin trees and the marketplaces, and its build script needs their directories; the Worker serves none of them.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from the record 4a8bb2d9 (mailto:alex@kesling.co, session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347) onto the lines it concerns, which moved when crates/clax-worker joined the root workspace and Bazel's build.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":29},"content_hash":"a3136e9431acf936f9444a0d85279791b41d2f0d18d4297f026145a23577be5b"},"summary":"Link clax-embedded in the Worker instead of embedding web/dist itself","supersedes":"4a8bb2d935ba0b2a0a12a635c827c1b42ff2b83c762c04b709bce74179259b42","tags":["worker","layout","revisit:clax-embedded splits its web UI from the other embeds","session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
